+The values `1.0` and `10` remain **provisional screening heuristics**. Estimator
+benchmarking and validation of that operational screening policy are distinct
+claims (`ext1-1`). For a generating GEV with location `mu`, scale `sigma>0`
+and standardized true quantile `z_p`, `q_p=mu+sigma*z_p`. Relative error
+`(qhat_p-q_p)/abs(q_p)` changes with location even when standardized estimation
+error is unchanged. Passing one location/scale choice therefore cannot validate
+a count-only rule for arbitrary discharge regimes. [argued: location-scale algebra]
+
+**Estimator benchmark, proposed and unexecuted.** All cell choices and numerical
+tolerances below await Astra model-validator review and owner acceptance before
+execution; none was ratified by G1 or external round 1. Use the unchanged
+xclim/SciPy fitting path, pin its GEV shape sign convention explicitly, and draw
+1,000 deterministically seeded standardized samples for each shape
+`{-0.2, 0.0, 0.2}` × usable-block count `{10, 18, 30, 60}`. Evaluate the current
+10-year upper (`p=0.9`) and 2-year lower (`p=0.5`) levels. The current 2-year
+minimum is thus the median of annual seven-day minima, not a claim about a more
+extreme lower-tail probability. Fit refusals count against the full 1,000 draws;
+error summaries are conditional on valid fits and report their denominator.
+
+For every fit report signed scale-normalized error
+`e_sigma=(qhat_p-q_p)/sigma`, its median, median absolute error and 90th-percentile
+absolute error. This measure is location-invariant and uses **generating** scale,
+never fitted scale as an error denominator. Proposed benchmark pass criteria
+are valid-fit rate at least 95%, absolute median `e_sigma` at most 0.10, and
+90th-percentile `abs(e_sigma)` at most 0.50 (upper) or 0.25 (lower).
+
+For relative-error diagnostics reuse each standardized sample at generating
+scale one and locations `mu=rho-z_p`, for `rho=q_p/sigma` in
+`{0, 0.05, 0.5, 2, 10}`. These controlled offsets span zero, near-zero, and
+progressively larger signal relative to variation; they are sensitivity cases,
+**not empirically established discharge-regime frequencies or a representative
+basin sample**. Refit the translated samples to expose numerical non-equivariance
+and require scale-error summaries to remain consistent with the same translated
+draws: proposed paired `e_sigma` tolerance `1e-6` absolute and unchanged fit-validity
+classification, both reviewed before execution. Report every deviation, with no
+silent optimizer retuning to pass the equivalence diagnostic.
+Report all signed/absolute relative summaries wherever `rho!=0`; at zero record
+`undefined` and the scale error, never epsilon-divide or silently exclude the case.
+The GEV samples can contain negative values: these are mathematical estimator
+fixtures, not generated discharge; do not truncate them and change the model.
